dialogue cohesion_knight_sage
title: The third watch
trigger: Cohesion knight sage level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker knight knight
speaker sage sage

node open commander
  It is past the middle of the night. The Knight is still on watch at the edge of the firelight, shield grounded, and the Sage has come out with a blanket and a cup and no intention of going back.
  -> third

node third sage
  That's your third watch running, Knight. On the road we'd call that a slow knot. Not tied yet. Just a matter of time.
  -> sleep

node sleep knight
  I'll sleep when the road's quiet. It isn't. There's something two hills back that keeps not quite following us. Somebody has to stand before the camp.
  -> before

node before sage
  Somebody. Not the same somebody every night. A tired shield is a door left open. Commander, you're the one the Knight listens to.
  * The Knight sleeps tonight. The Sage takes the watch. -> swap
    do: AddCohesion knight sage 10
    do: AddTrust knight -3
    do: SetFlag knight_sage:watch_swapped
  * Split it. Half the night each, and sit together at the change. -> split
    do: AddCohesion knight sage 6
    do: SetFlag knight_sage:watch_split
  * The Knight keeps the watch. That's what the shield is for. -> keeps
    do: AddCohesion knight sage -4
    do: AddTrust sage -2
    do: SetFlag knight_sage:watch_kept
  * I took the Knight's watch once, the way the Knight took it for us at the ford. Now the Sage takes it. -> ford
    if: FlagSet knight:line_watch
    do: AddCohesion knight sage 8
    do: AddTrust knight 2
    do: SetFlag knight_sage:watch_ford

node swap knight
  Fine. The shield stays here, by your foot, and you wake me if anything on that hill so much as coughs. Promise, Sage.
  -> ends

node split sage
  Half each. I'll take the second half. Healers are good at the hour before dawn. That's when people need us.
  -> ends

node keeps sage
  Then I'll sit here and keep the watch company. You can't order me to bed, Knight. You're not the Commander.
  -> ends

node ford knight
  The ford. I'd nearly forgotten that was the same thing. All right. Two watches to give back, then, and I'll take the third.
  -> ends

node ends knight
  You've a clean end to tie on that cord, and I've a second line on the rim I can't get past the first word of. Both of us stuck at the last bit. Do you ever think we're afraid to finish?
  * No knots for anyone here. The Knight stands before, so the cord stays clean. -> clean
    if: FlagSet sage:cord_down
    do: AddCohesion knight sage 10
    do: AddTrust sage 2
    do: SetFlag knight_sage:ends_clean
  * When we reach the holds, the Sage looks at the sister first, before anyone. -> sister
    if: FlagSet knight:sister_promised
    do: AddCohesion knight sage 8
    do: AddTrust knight 2
    do: SetFlag knight_sage:ends_sister
  * Trade. The Sage helps pick the Knight's second line. The Knight helps pick the last knot. -> trade
    do: AddCohesion knight sage 8
    do: SetFlag knight_sage:ends_traded
  * Those ends are each of yours to finish alone. -> alone
    do: AddCohesion knight sage 2
    do: AddTrust sage -2
    do: SetFlag knight_sage:ends_alone

node clean sage
  A clean cord because there's a shield in front of it. I'll take that. But you sleep sometimes, Knight. A shield on its face in the mud covers nobody.
  -> close

node sister sage
  First. A water carrier, you said. I'll know her colour before she's set the bucket down. And then I'll want to meet the stubborn one with the spears in the well.
  -> close

node trade knight
  You pick my word, I pick your knot. That's a fair trade. Fair warning, Sage, I'll pick something plain. Holds don't do fancy.
  -> close

node alone knight
  Alone. Yes. Some things are. I'll stand my watch, and you count your knots, and we'll both pretend we're not counting each other.
  -> close

node close commander
  The blanket ends up round both their shoulders. The Knight's shield stays grounded between them, and the thing two hills back never does follow.
